+---
+
+#### 1. Mandarin speech is excluded before any analysis (new)
+
+*Item added.* The registration treats every utterance of an Indigenous-language clip as speech in
+that language. TITV clips contain Mandarin interviews, whose subtitle is a transcript, not a
+translation. Such an utterance in the reference set is unreachable by Arm A by construction and
+reachable by Arm B, so it inflates the primary statistic of Amendment 3 item 6; in §6.2 it carries
+the wrong language.
+
+*What it becomes.* An utterance is excluded as Mandarin if either (a) an audio-language judgement
+by `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` (`pipeline/analysis/lid_gemini.py`; audio only, the first 30 s of a longer utterance, no
+subtitle, transcript or video; temperature 0; no thinking; prompt fixed by its SHA-256 in the
+provenance) answers
+`mandarin`, `mixed` or `no_speech`, or (b) the normalized edit distance between the Han characters
+of the utterance's subtitle and of the overlapping Whisper segments is at most 0.4
+(`mandarin_filter.py`). Kept: `not_chinese` and `other_chinese`. `other_chinese` (Gemini's
+answer for Hokkien or Hakka) is kept because on Study 1 Gemini gave it to 397 utterances of
+Indigenous-language news, far more than such news plausibly contains, and the author heard both
+decided `other_chinese` items as not Mandarin: the answer marks unfamiliar non-Mandarin speech.
+An utterance without a valid Gemini answer is excluded and counted. Sensitivity: `mixed` kept. The
+model's outputs are frozen with the run; the model judges language, not force. Counts per language
+and per half are reported. It applies to every language: to Paiwan throughout §6.1, and to all six
+languages in every utterance-level analysis that compares languages (§6.2 and the cross-language
+retrieval of Chapter 5), whose primary versions exclude Mandarin; the versions without the
+exclusion are sensitivity analyses. Gemini is therefore run on the utterances of all 216 clips and
+of the 84 added Paiwan clips. Mandarin utterances are still labeled (§3 item 8), for item 8.
+
+*Why, measured on Study 1.* The text match alone misses Mandarin: Whisper often translates Mandarin
+speech into English, and the assigned subtitle line is often the neighbouring one (Amendment 7 applies no
+offset). The author listened blind to 47 Study 1 utterances (`listen_sample.py`, seeds 20261015
+and 20261016, 2026-10-14): where Gemini answered `mandarin`, the author heard Mandarin 20 times, mixed once,
+not Mandarin twice (14 undecidable); where Gemini answered anything else, the author heard
+Mandarin 0 times. By Gemini's answers about 65% of Study 1 utterances are Mandarin.
+
+#### 2. The Chinese directive criterion (Amendment 3 item 1)
+
+*Item clarified.* "The rule-based directive criterion of Study 2, unchanged" cannot run on Chinese:
+it is a rule over English sentence mood. *What it becomes:* its category-for-category Chinese
+counterpart on explicit markers, `pipeline/analysis/directive_zh.py` at commit `f40d4dc` (IMP: 請 +
+verb; HORT: 讓我們一起, 吧-final with a first-person-plural or 大家 subject; NEG.IMP: clause-initial
+不要/別/請勿 ...; DEONTIC: addressee or audience subject + 應該/必須/務必/一定要, plural addressee + 要;
+reported speech and questions excluded), applied after item 1. Revised on Study 1 only.
+
+#### 3. The registered route comparison is kept and reported; its expected size is stated
+
+*Item recorded, not changed.* Amendment 3 items 1 to 7 and Amendment 6 items 1 and 2 are computed
+as registered, with items 1, 2 and 4 of this amendment, on all 120 Paiwan clips (item 4).
+
+*Expectation stated in advance.* After item 1, Study 1's Paiwan subtitles satisfy the criterion of
+item 2 in 0 to 2 of 545 utterances (the rest of Study 1's directive hits are Mandarin speech). The
+reference set is therefore expected to hold about 0 to 10 utterances. *Rules:* the primary result
+of Amendment 3 item 6 becomes the case table (each reference utterance of the scoring half with its
+route); the fraction reached by B and not A, with its day-cluster bootstrap, is reported only if
+the scoring half holds at least 10 reference utterances, and otherwise is stated as not estimable.
+If the seed half holds no reference utterance, Arm B has no seed and is not run; this is reported.
+
+#### 4. All 120 Paiwan clips (amends Amendment 6 item 4, Scope)
+
+*What it was.* The 84 undrawn Paiwan clips entered Arm C only. *What it becomes.* For Paiwan, the
+reference set, Arms A, B and T and the experiment of item 5 use all 120 clips of the 12 days. The
+seed/scoring split stays at the day level; inference remains over days. Labels (§3 item 8) are not
+run on the 84 clips, and the 84 clips enter no analysis outside §6.1. *Why:* item 3; whole days involve no
+selection (the argument of Amendment 6 item 4).
+
+#### 5. A judged directive experiment replaces Arm C and the listener checks (new primary for §6.1)
+
+*What it was.* Arm C (Amendment 6 item 3) ranked -u candidates by similarity to reference-set
+seeds and scored them against the reference standard; the listener checked 40 tokens from the
+route cells and 10 from Arm C (Amendment 3 item 8, Amendment 6 item 5). With a reference set of
+about 0 to 10, neither has seeds or cells. *What it becomes:*
+
+**Question.** Among Paiwan utterances carrying a form that may mark a directive (the hortative
+`ari`, the prohibitive `maya`, the imperative suffixes `-u` and `-i`), do non-text cues help decide
+whether the utterance is a directive, beyond its text, form included? And how often is a
+directive carried by none of these forms?
+
+**Pool** (`form_candidates.py`): Paiwan utterances of the 120 clips kept by item 1. Form class
+from the transcription tokens (Amendment 4 B2 normalization, then lowercased with non-letters
+removed): `marker` if a token is `ari` or
+matches `ma[jy]a`; otherwise `suffix` if a token of two or more letters ends in `u` or `i`
+(Amendment 6 item 3, extended to `-i`) and is not one of the 51 function words of
+`paiwan_suffix_stoplist.json`; otherwise `none`. The stoplist is fixed by rule on One Hundred
+Paiwan Texts (FormosanBank commit 52524b1): u/i-final word forms occurring at least 15 times with
+no token glossed `imp` or `hort` (`paiwan_stoplist.py`). There it moves the share of
+directive-glossed tokens among u/i-final tokens from 1:20 to 1:5. It comes from narrative text in
+one dialect; news Paiwan may have function words it misses, which lowers precision only. Cue, for enrichment only: the subtitle
+text within the utterance +- 3 s contains a loose marker (請 要 吧 不要 別 一起 應該 必須 務必 記得
+趕快 快點 讓我們 來 可以 不可以 不能 千萬). Strata: `marker`, `suffix_cue`, `suffix_nocue`, `none_cue`,
+`none_nocue` (not drawn). Neither cue nor stratum is a label or a model input.
+
+**Draw** (`draw_annotation.py`, `default_rng(20261018)`): quotas marker 50, suffix_cue 100,
+suffix_nocue 60, none_cue 30 (240). A stratum smaller than its quota is taken whole and the
+shortfall goes to suffix_cue, then suffix_nocue, then marker, then none_cue. Inclusion
+probabilities are kept. Batch 1: 50 items with the same stratum shares; batch 2: the other 190;
+batch 3: 40 repeats, simple random, judged at least 7 days after batch 2.
+
+**Judgement.** One Paiwan-speaking annotator, offline page (`make_annotation_kit.py`): video from
+2 s before to 2 s after the utterance, the subtitle band (75 to 90% of the frame height) blacked
+out, one key per item: 1 directive (the speaker asks the addressee, or a group including the
+speaker, to do or not to do something: command, request, urging, invitation, reminder,
+prohibition), 2 not directive, 3 cannot tell. Answer 3 is excluded from the models and counted.
+**Go/no-go:** batch 2 is judged only if batch 1 has at least 3 answers 1. Otherwise the experiment
+stops here, the count is reported, and any later attempt on other material is exploratory.
+Intra-rater agreement: Cohen's kappa on batch 3. One annotator: no inter-rater figure exists, and
+the write-up says so.
+
+**Feature blocks**, all frozen, computed per utterance:
+- T, text: the Paiwan transcription as in Amendment 4 B2 (XLM-R mean-pooled embedding and TF-IDF),
+  plus the form class as indicators (marker / suffix / none, and `ari` versus `maya`).
+- A, audio: Whisper large-v3 encoder mean over the utterance; the 15 prosodic features (item 6, point 3).
+- V, vision, two blocks:
+  - K, kinematics: the kinematic primary of item 6, point 1 (missing tight frames: training-fold mean plus
+    a missing indicator).
+  - Fa, face: OpenFace 3.0 (code commit and weights recorded at first run) on frames sampled at
+    10 per second inside the utterance, taking in each frame the largest detected face (no active
+    speaker detection exists; the largest face is a proxy for the speaker, stated). Per
+    utterance: mean and standard deviation of every action-unit intensity it outputs, of gaze yaw
+    and pitch, and of head yaw, pitch and roll; plus the share of sampled frames with a face.
+    Utterances with a face in fewer than half of the sampled frames get the training-fold mean
+    and a missing indicator. The share of judged items with a face is reported: a voice-over
+    speaker is usually not on screen, and then no visual block describes the speaker.
+- F, framing: the 8 framing measures of item 6, point 4, as a control.
+
+**Models.** Logistic regression, L2, C = 1.0, sample weights = inverse inclusion probability.
+These settings are fixed a priori, not tuned: Study 1 has no judged directives to tune on, and
+Study 3 may not be used for tuning. Inside
+each training fold, every block is standardized and reduced by PCA to min(16, n_train - 1)
+components, so that blocks enter with equal dimension (K and Fa are separate blocks; V = K+Fa).
+Models: T; T+A; T+K; T+Fa; T+V; T+A+V; F alone.
+Cross-validation: leave one broadcast day out (12 folds); out-of-fold scores pooled.
+
+**Primary items.** The models are trained and evaluated on the items of strata marker,
+suffix_cue and suffix_nocue only; the none_cue items enter no model and are reported
+descriptively.
+
+**Primary statistic.** On the primary items: weighted
+AUC(T+A+V) minus weighted AUC(T) on the pooled out-of-fold scores,
+with a paired day-cluster bootstrap (12 days resampled, 10,000 resamples,
+`default_rng(20261017)`), 95% percentile interval and one-sided p for a positive difference.
+**Secondary:** the same difference on the suffix items only (the forms that are ambiguous); T+A
+minus T; T+V minus T; T+K minus T (gesture and body); T+Fa minus T (gaze, head and face); F
+alone against T+V (a vision gain that F alone matches is a framing effect, not a gesture or face
+effect); the same differences on the items with a face only; weighted AP for each model; the
+directive share per form class and per stratum (weighted); the none_cue items: the share judged
+directive, reported descriptively as directives carried by none of the four forms (enriched,
+so it bounds nothing in the population; stated). If batches 1 and 2 yield fewer than 15 answers 1, all of this is
+reported descriptively, without p-values.
+
+**Text-classifier baselines.** CLM-8B (Contrastive Language Models,
+`github.com/Contrastive-LM/CLM`, Apache 2.0; a frozen Qwen3-8B encoder with a trained projection
+head, contrastive state-action objective; served by the repository's `clm-serve` over vLLM
+pooling; package, weight and backbone revisions recorded at first run) is a **registered
+secondary text baseline**. Question, typed `Choice`, fixed wording: "Is the speaker asking the
+listener (or a group that includes the speaker) to do something or not to do something, as in a
+command, request, urging, invitation, reminder or prohibition?" Options "yes, a directive" / "no,
+not a directive"; score = probability of the first. No examples, tuning or re-wording. Two inputs
+scored separately: (a) the Chinese subtitle text within the utterance +- 3 s (the human
+translation); (b) the Paiwan transcription. It is not trained on the judgements, so its score on
+every judged item is used as is. Reported: weighted AUC and AP of CLM(a) and CLM(b) on the primary
+items, and AUC(T+A+V) minus AUC(CLM(a)) and minus AUC(CLM(b)) with the same paired day-cluster
+bootstrap, overall and by stratum (input (a) reads the same window as the enrichment cue, so
+CLM(a) is expected to be advantaged on the `cue` strata; stated in advance). TypeSafe AI's Jev,
+the closed counterpart with the same interface, stays exploratory (Amendment 6 item 6a): run only
+after the statistics above are recorded, never a label or part of block T.
+
+#### 6. Choices left open in §2 and §3, fixed
+
+1. *Kinematic primary (§2 item 6):* the 14-dimensional composition-robust variant on tight frames
+   (at most 2 persons, tracked body at least 12% of the frame); an utterance needs at least 8 tight
+   frames. Secondary: 18d tight, 14d and 18d residualized on the 3 shot-block PCs, 9d
+   gesture-conditioned, 18d full.
+2. *Lift (§2 item 5):* units are labeled utterances within one shot, eligible under 1; top-1 cosine
+   retrieval per ordered language pair; hit if labels match; chance = the query label's share among
+   the target language's utterances; pair lift = mean(hit - chance); class lift = mean over its
+   ordered pairs. Primary: Middle minus Long, one-sided, day-cluster bootstrap (days within
+   language, 10,000 resamples). Short descriptive.
+3. *Arm B modalities (Amendment 6 item 1):* audio (Whisper large-v3 encoder mean), prosody (15
+   features, standardized within language, NaN to the language mean), kinematics (1); per-query
+   z-scored similarities, fused by the mean over the modalities available.
+4. *Framing measures:* the 8-feature shot block of `analysis/q10` over the utterance's pose frames.
+5. *Labels (§3 items 8 to 9):* `label_units.py` at commit `0c3932f`; clip prompt identical to Study 1;
+   utterance prompt with three wording changes; temperature 0; primary
+   `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001`; second model `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` on all units; self-consistency
+   on 334 utterances per language (`draw_perturbation_sample.py`, seed 20261014) under offsets 0.25
+   and 0.75 and one category-order permutation. These measure reliability, not validity.
+6. *Arm A on the tier:* `armA.py`; an utterance is in A if `ari` or `ma[jy]a` occurs in its
+   concatenated `armA_pwn` phones, unwindowed; reproduces `q21` exactly on NTU.
+
+#### 7. Withdrawn
+
+The audio criterion checks (§3 item 9 iii): their source `data/output_gemini/` does not exist for
+Study 3 and speaker change is unavailable (Amendment 8 item 4); a replacement would be a new
+hypothesis. The human checks of Amendment 3 item 8 and Amendment 6 item 5: replaced by item 5.
